From eed6e56b45db4a001d837ecf7956c10c5a503c0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Matuszewski <xanewok@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 20:20:31 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/15] common : sampling: keep the top-k prefilter under a
 lazy grammar and the reasoning budget

The prefilter of set_logits was off whenever the sampler had a grammar or a reasoning budget, which a
tool-calling request with thinking always has, so the target sampled over the full vocab. Now it is decided
per draw: the first draw of common_sampler_sample takes the chain's top-k straight from the logits unless
something ahead of the chain reads the row, i.e. the budget is FORCING (full-row mask) or a grammar is applied
first (grammar_first with the grammar applying). Outside FORCING the budget is a passthrough; the grammar gated
off during thinking, or lazy and awaiting its trigger, changes nothing; with grammar_first == false the grammar
checks the one drawn token. The grammar-reject resample still reads and masks the full row, so the law
P(x) = c(x) 1[x in G] + (1 - c(G)) c'(x) is unchanged. The rejection verify reads only the post-chain
candidates and is unaffected.

test-sampling-prefilter (model path: vocab, chat template, and real output rows with synthetic logits):
Qwen3.5-4B, codex-like tools + thinking, temp 1, top-k 20 / top-p 0.95 / min-p 0.05. Per-seed token streams of
single draws, trajectories across the trigger and forced budget, and 3-draft rejection verifies are
byte-identical to the previous commit (300 seeds each); chi-square against the host law passes in every state,
and a prefilter that also serves the resample fails it (p = 3e-89). Mutants of this change (resample
prefiltered, forcing ignored, grammar_first ignored, k - 1) each fail the test. Per draw: thinking
325 -> 86 us, prose awaiting the trigger 299 -> 83 us; grammar-active draws are dominated by the full-vocab
mask of rejected draws (~33 ms per reject) either way.
